From 3d5a3bf8794b3bbfb42bc58068177f58fcba693b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:41:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 33/41] fix(done): close review-only reviewer's attached wisp
 on no-MR completion (gfork-4sz)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A require_review=true reviewer (formula mol-polecat-review-pr) runs gt done on
the no-MR completion path. gfork-06a made that path reachable for review-only
beads (isNoMergeTask=true skips the verified_push gate), so the base bead is now
force-closed via ForceCloseWithReason — bypassing its open attached wisp. That
resolves the *blocking* half of gfork-4sz.

But the no-MR path never closed the wisp itself, and updateAgentStateOnDone (run
later via notifyWitness) then skips its own wisp-close because the base bead is
already terminal — leaving the wisp orphaned/open. A reviewer's gt done should
leave nothing dangling.

Fix: extract the wisp-close logic into closeAttachedWisp (step descendants +
force-close the wisp root, ErrNotFound-tolerant) and call it from both the
no-MR close path (after the base bead force-closes) and updateAgentStateOnDone
(behavior-preserving refactor). Auto-resolves the wisp on review-only completion.

Hermetic tests (internal/cmd/done_review_wisp_test.go): closeAttachedWisp closes
the wisp + step descendants for a review-only bead, and is a safe no-op when the
bead has no attached molecule. Full loop green (gofumpt/vet/build clean; new
tests pass under -race). internal/cmd's 20 pre-existing failures (macOS unsigned-
binary SIGKILL + bd-subprocess, gfork-94k class) verified identical with this
change stashed — zero new failures.

